===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|cok|id=rooster}}, from {{inh|en|ang|coc}}, {{m|ang|cocc|t=cock, male bird}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*kokk}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*kukkaz|t=cock}}, probably of {{onomatopoeic|en|title=onomatopoeic}} origin.

Cognate with {{cog|dum|cocke|t=cock, male bird}} and {{cog|non|kokkr}} {{gloss|"cock"; whence {{cog|da|kok|t=cock}}, dialectal {{cog|sv|kokk|t=cock}}}}. Reinforced by {{cog|fro|coc|}}, also of imitative origin. The sense "penis" is attested since at least the 1610s, with the compound {{m|en|pillicock||penis}} attested since 1325.

